# macOS folder metadata
.DS_Store

# Visual brainstorming companion mockups
.superpowers/

# Compiled backend binary (make build / make run)
/bin/

# The book editions (book/how-money-moves.{epub,pdf}) are intentionally checked
# in so they can be linked and downloaded directly. Rebuild with book/build.sh.

# The ISO 20022 message schemas the golden-file check validates against.
#
# iso20022/testdata/README.md says this directory "is not committed: the schemas
# are redistributed under ISO's terms and are not this repository's to vendor",
# and until now nothing enforced it. A developer who downloads them and runs
# `git add -A` — which is what every plan in docs/superpowers/plans tells them to
# do — vendors them by accident, and the rule is broken by the workflow the
# repository itself prescribes.
iso20022/testdata/xsd/

# The compiled server binary. `go build` with no -o drops it here under the
# module's name, and `git add -A` — which is what every plan in
# docs/superpowers/plans tells a developer to do — then commits 17 MB of it.
# That is exactly what happened in Task 17.2, and it rode along in every commit
# after it until the history was rewritten to take it out. Same failure mode as
# iso20022/testdata/xsd above: a rule nothing enforced, broken by the workflow
# this repository prescribes.
/server
